**How to implement.** An experiment holds a scan, a role, a session and notes, and the draft builds a scan of any number of axes and blocks (001 §K '`Experiment` = one recorded run: a setup reference and a scan …; a capture (T / R, from the detectors); a role …; a session'; 001 §E notes live in the experiment's file; the S9.1 brief: today's single-variable experiments are one-variable scans). This is one step because the record's fields change every consumer at once (the step 261 precedent). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`. (a) `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `{ id : ExperimentId; setup : SetupReference; scan : ExperimentScan; role : ExperimentRole; sessionOpt : SessionName option; notes : ExperimentNotes; dataFileOpt : DataAttachment option }`: `varied`, `measurement`, `range` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt` are the scan's (step 287), and `VariedElement` (step 261) and `Experiment.variedLabel` are deleted, `ScanAxis` being their successor. `description` keeps its two texts for the scans today's experiments are: one block of one axis is `<axis describe>, capture <capture.label>` (today's varied text exactly), and one block of no axis is step 261's `Dark line on setup <setup.describe>, capture <capture.label>`; any other scan is its blocks' texts joined by `; `, a block's text being its axes' `describe`s joined by ` × ` and then `, capture <capture.label>` (`Dark line, capture <label>` for a block of no axis). (b) `ExperimentDraft` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentDraft`) keeps its fields, the edited axis being `elementId`, `elementLabel`, `variable` and `range`, and gains `outerAxes : ScanAxis list` (the axes of the current block before the edited one, outermost first) and `closedBlocks : ScanBlock list` (the blocks before the current one), both `[]` in `empty`. `member this.axisOpt : ScanAxis option` is the edited axis once an element and a variable are chosen; `member this.scanOpt : ExperimentScan option` is, with it, `closedBlocks` followed by the block of `outerAxes` and the edited axis read on `measurement`, with `sourceWaveLengthOpt`. `ExperimentCollection.canCommit` (`Experiments.fs:canCommit`) matches `draft.axisOpt`, its answers unchanged. (c) `addScanAxis (c : ExperimentCollection) : ExperimentCollection`: with an edited axis, the draft's `outerAxes` gain it and its `elementId`, `elementLabel` and `variable` clear, its range becoming `VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1`; otherwise `c` unchanged. `addScanBlock (c : ExperimentCollection) : ExperimentCollection`: with an edited axis, `closedBlocks` gain the block of `outerAxes` and it read on `measurement`, `outerAxes` empties and the edited axis clears as above; otherwise `c` unchanged. `chooseElement` keeps `outerAxes` and `closedBlocks`, and `newDraft` clears them with the rest. (d) `commit` (`Experiments.fs:commit`, step 261's signature kept) builds from `draft.scanOpt`: an edited experiment takes the setup and the scan and keeps its role, session, notes and data file; an appended one is `ScienceRun`, with no session, `ExperimentNotes.none` and no data file. `commitOverSetups` (step 275) folds it as before. (e) `edit` (`Experiments.fs:edit`) splits the experiment's scan back: `closedBlocks` are every block but the last, the last block's capture is `measurement`, its axes but the last are `outerAxes`, and its last axis is the edited one (none for a block of no axis), with the scan's `sourceWaveLengthOpt`; so editing then committing gives the experiment back. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `requestedWavelengthsOf` (`OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:requestedWavelengthsOf`) answers `SweptWavelengths` from the lowest `min` to the highest `max` of the scan's `VaryWaveLength` axes, each end through `toWaveLength Nanometer` as `requestedWavelengthsFor` reads one range, and `FixedWavelength fixedWavelength` when no axis varies the wavelength; `requestedWavelengthsFor` is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) validates through `MeasuredData.validateAgainstExperiment` (`MeasuredData.fs:validateAgainstExperiment`, unchanged) with the one axis's variable and range for a scan of one block of one axis, and with no variable and `VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1` for a scan of one block of no axis (the range every dark line held, step 50); for any other scan it reads nothing and answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` `an X,Y data file holds one variable, and the scan varies <n> in <m> block(s)` (S9.2's profiles map such files). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` (steps 146, 261): under schema version 1, `experiment` holds exactly `id`, `setup`, `scan` (an object holding exactly `blocks`, an array, and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`), `role` (an integer from 1 to 7), `sessionOpt` (`null` or a string holding a non-white-space character), `notes` (a string) and `dataFileOpt`; the version stays 1, because no kit of the old shape exists outside test output (.spec-md §7). (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `chartForExperiment` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForExperiment`) runs `chartForRun` over the axis, the capture and the wavelength of a scan of one block of one axis, and answers the empty chart for any other scan until step 293 draws every scan. `SolverHandoffView.fs` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) calls `loadAndValidate` as before and nothing in it changes. No message, view or other member changes in this step. (6) Every fixture that builds an `Experiment` builds its scan as `ExperimentScan.oneAxis` of the `ScanAxis` its `VariedElement` and range made, with the capture and wavelength it set, or as `ExperimentScan.darkLine` of its capture for a dark line, and sets `role = ScienceRun`, `sessionOpt = None` and `notes = ExperimentNotes.none`, every fact keeping its assertions: in `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `KitLibraryTests`, `ExperimentCopyTests`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`, `SetupTests`, `SetupModelTests`, `KitWindowModelTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `InverseConstructorTests` and `KitWindowTests`, whichever of them build one; one the closing build finds anywhere else is re-pointed by the same rule. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a committed experiment is a one-axis scan of the draft, a science run with no session and no notes`: `commit` of `Bench` revision 1 after `chooseElement` of `lp2` (R1, 0…90°, 10 points, capture T, 632.8 nm) appends an experiment whose scan is `oneAxis` of that axis, read in T at 632.8 nm, `ScienceRun`, no session and `ExperimentNotes.none`, its description the text `an experiment description mentions the element, the variable, and the capture` reads; and `an added axis and an added block commit as one multi-variable scan, and editing splits it back`: `chooseElement` of the sample (R2 over 20…60°, 3 points), `addScanAxis`, `chooseElement` of the sample (R1 over 0…90°, 2 points), capture both, `addScanBlock`, `chooseElement` of `lp2` (R1 over 0…67.5°, 4 points), capture T, then `commit`, appends one experiment whose scan has the blocks [R2 × R1, both] and [R1, T] in that order; `edit` of it gives a draft whose `closedBlocks`, `outerAxes`, edited axis and capture are those, and `commit` again leaves the experiment equal; `addScanAxis` of a draft with nothing chosen changes nothing. `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 261): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` also round-trips E1 with that two-block scan, `CalibrationRun`, the session `Day 1` and the notes `LR was re-seated`; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses `role` 0, `sessionOpt` `""` and an experiment without `scan`. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed` also finds that a scan whose two blocks vary the wavelength over 300…500 nm and 400…700 nm requests 300…700 nm. `ExperimentDataProxyTests` (step 135) gains `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan`: over its mock data proxy, the built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue`) and slots whose detector slot is bound to `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, an experiment of one axis whose range holds every abscissa of the canned intensity series answers that series, and the same experiment with a second axis answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming 2 variables and 1 block.

**Acceptance.** After Experiment v2 lands, `Experiment` MUST hold `scan`, `role`, `sessionOpt` and `notes` in place of `varied`, `measurement`, `range` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`, `VariedElement` MUST be gone, the draft MUST build a scan of several axes and blocks through `addScanAxis` and `addScanBlock`, `edit` MUST split it back, and the experiment file MUST round-trip it under schema version 1; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a committed experiment is a one-axis scan of the draft, a science run with no session and no notes`, `an added axis and an added block commit as one multi-variable scan, and editing splits it back` and `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` and `requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
